# Node Types

Three fundamental node types form the building blocks of your tunnel architecture.

{% grid cols=3 %}
{% card title="Entry" icon="entry" description="Your machine where traffic enters the tunnel chain. Creates a TUN interface and runs an interactive REPL." %}
```bash
wallhack entry --listen :PORT
```
{% /card %}

{% card title="Relay (Optional)" icon="relay" description="Optional intermediate host that forwards traffic deeper into the network. Connects upstream and listens downstream. Not required for simple entry-to-exit tunnels." %}
```bash
wallhack relay --connect HOST:PORT --listen :PORT
```
{% /card %}

{% card title="Exit" icon="exit" description="End of the tunnel chain. Unwraps packets and sends them to the target network via syscalls." %}
```bash
wallhack exit --connect HOST:PORT
```
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

The node role is declared explicitly via subcommand. Transport direction (`--listen` / `--connect`) is independent of role — entry and exit nodes can either listen or connect, enabling reverse tunnels. **wallhack can operate with just entry and exit nodes** — relays are only needed when intermediate pivoting is required.

{% separator /%}

# Command Flags

Two primary flags control the behavior of wallhack nodes.

{% card title="--listen :PORT" icon="terminal" %}
Accept incoming connections on the specified port
{% /card %}

{% card title="--connect HOST:PORT" icon="terminal" %}
Establish outgoing connection to specified host and port
{% /card %}

{% separator /%}

# Additional Flags

{% grid cols=2 %}
{% card title="--api ADDRESS" icon="terminal" %}
Enable REST API on entry nodes (e.g., `127.0.0.1:6566`)
{% /card %}

{% card title="--api-user / --api-pass" icon="terminal" %}
Basic authentication for the REST API
{% /card %}

{% card title="--cert / --key" icon="terminal" %}
TLS certificate and private key for encrypted connections
{% /card %}

{% card title="--ca" icon="terminal" %}
CA certificate for mutual TLS authentication
{% /card %}

{% card title="--dns" icon="terminal" %}
DNS server for target resolution
{% /card %}

{% card title="--exit-id" icon="terminal" %}
Identifier for stable TUN device naming on exit nodes
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}
